{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghhoAd8XiYeqHMbPbFjH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"While the hub check runs, writing the four feedback sections into the About & Credits screen so they ship in the game."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":802,"cache_read_input_tokens":379932,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":802},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bb246035-72d8-4ccb-80ef-f75810865350","uuid":"a94f96dd-06f1-47a2-9c65-b807638dc853","timestamp":"2026-11-04T10:08:45.482Z","request_id":"req_011CghhoAHnJtKscCoFs7Fmu"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghhoAd8XiYeqHMbPbFjH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01N3xEfb9iWe9saoQuBppKuE","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='src/60-text.js'\ns=open(p).read()\na=\"  ['h', 'THANKS'],\\n  ['w', 'To the players who ride the rails at the speed of the snow.'],\\n];\"\nb=\"\"\"  ['h', 'TESTING FEEDBACK'],\n  ['w', 'About fifteen issues were caught: a crash on Room 7, a black frame from the Comic cel filter, two Rime gates that could lock a run, a junction that committed by itself, and a camera inside a wall. Five were game-breaking. The most useful test was the Node playthrough of every area; the least useful was frame-by-frame screenshots.'],\n  ['s', 0],\n  ['h', 'ENGINE FEEDBACK'],\n  ['w', 'Liked most: the 3D module\\\\'s fixed cameras and the card-drawn rigs, with the pause menu, settings and saves for free. Guessed wrong: particle argument orders, pen box centres, the cel filter options and the menu close. Built myself: the rail walker, the Whiteout AI, the persona abilities, the bot. No engine files were changed.'],\n  ['s', 0],\n  ['h', 'PROMPT FEEDBACK'],\n  ['w', 'Liked: concrete deliverables, file names and checks, and the one-command test rule. Confusing: the plan is about 2,100 lines and asks for engine patches and seven full personas, so the scope had to be cut to fit. Change: give the plan a must, should and cut list and a size budget.'],\n  ['s', 0],\n  ['h', 'THANKS'],\n  ['w', 'To the players who ride the rails at the speed of the snow.'],\n];\"\"\"\nassert s.count(a)==1\ns=s.replace(a,b); open(p,'w').write(s); print('ok')\nEOF\ncat out/hub-check.log 2>/dev/null | tail -4","description":"Add the four feedback sections to the in-game About screen"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":802,"cache_read_input_tokens":379932,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":802},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bb246035-72d8-4ccb-80ef-f75810865350","uuid":"fa28e79b-fe2f-472c-855e-ed52388bc4eb","timestamp":"2026-11-04T10:08:48.132Z","request_id":"req_011CghhoAHnJtKscCoFs7Fmu","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01N3xEfb9iWe9saoQuBppKuE":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-023153__x696bb3/work/Skiller7-Killer7-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-023153 && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='src/60-text.js'\ns=open(p).read()\na=\"  ['h', 'THANKS'],\\n  ['w', 'To the players who ride the rails at the speed of the snow.'],\\n];\"\nb=\"\"\"  ['h', 'TESTING FEEDBACK'],\n  ['w', 'About fifteen issues were caught: a crash on Room 7, a black frame from the Comic cel filter, two Rime gates that could lock a run, a junction that committed by itself, and a camera inside a wall. Five were game-breaking. The most useful test was the Node playthrough of every area; the least useful was frame-by-frame screenshots.'],\n  ['s', 0],\n  ['h', 'ENGINE FEEDBACK'],\n  ['w', 'Liked most: the 3D module\\\\'s fixed cameras and the card-drawn rigs, with the pause menu, settings and saves for free. Guessed wrong: particle argument orders, pen box centres, the cel filter options and the menu close. Built myself: the rail walker, the Whiteout AI, the persona abilities, the bot. No engine files were changed.'],\n  ['s', 0],\n  ['h', 'PROMPT FEEDBACK'],\n  ['w', 'Liked: concrete deliverables, file names and checks, and the one-command test rule. Confusing: the plan is about 2,100 lines and asks for engine patches and seven full personas, so the scope had to be cut to fit. Change: give the plan a must, should and cut list and a size budget.'],\n  ['s', 0],\n  ['h', 'THANKS'],\n  ['w', 'To