{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghoDgtYYWvpLsSjXiJ1V","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The game is rebuilt with the new features, and the suite passes 156 of 156 checks. I can't confirm that every TASK.md feature is fully implemented, so I'm not claiming the goal is met. Here is what changed and what's still short.\n\n**Closed since the last reply**\n- **AI Hub result, end to end:** a mock hub now receives the Echo Run result. The suite runs this round as its last step.\n- **Attract on touch-only devices:** it now runs, as TASK.md asks. The attract timer also pauses while a hub session is active.\n- **Persona accessories:** goggles, scarves, moustaches and beards are drawn on the rig. This needed one engine patch, marked `S7 PATCH` in `engine/my-3d2dge.js`.\n- **Murmel and Pim:** two NPCs you talk to with the interact button. Pim gives the code to the service door on the stairs, and the door opens only when you enter it on the pad.\n- **Dossier:** notes on the rails fill a dossier in Room 7.\n- **Boss cutscene:** the Bellcaptain's intro is a camera cut with dialogue. Closing the dialogue skips it.\n- **Animation:** Whiteouts shiver while they laugh and sink into the snow when thawed. The skier crouches to brake.\n- **Comic cel filter:** I retested it, and it still blanks the screen, as does Pixel. I removed the Filter option from Settings. I couldn't check either filter on a real GPU.\n\n**Still short of \"every TASK.md feature\"**\n- **Mouse aiming and clicking:** wired through the engine's pointer capture, but the tests never exercise it, because headless Chromium can't lock the pointer.\n- **Cutscenes:** there is no general cutscene system. The only camera cut is the boss intro.\n- **Narrative depth:** two NPCs, two notes and one code door. PLAN.md's full set is not here.\n- **Art and animation:** props are pen-drawn. The new animations are small shivers, sinks and crouches. There is no new move set and no new character models.\n- **Scope:** three areas, about ten minutes of play. The plan called for 45–60 minutes.\n- **Title:** Skiller7 is the title PLAN.md gives. I did not run my own 50-title brainstorm.\n\n**Verification:** `node tests/run.mjs` passes 156 of 156 checks, including the bot playthrough of every area, the browser flows, touch-only detection, and the AI Hub round.\n\n**Files**\n- `Skiller7-Killer7-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-023153.html` (the single file)\n- `exit-interview.json` (parses; every field is answered)\n- `Skiller7-Killer7-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-023153/` (dev folder)\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 02:31:53\n- **Source:** Killer7\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and perspective:** shooter, on-rails action-adventure. Fixed cinematic rail cameras with hard cuts while moving, first person while aiming.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (2D engine and 3D module, commit 4390a98, with one S7 patch for accessories), three.js r182 and Rapier 0.19.3 from jsDelivr, AI Hub client 1.4.0 unmodified. Node 24 and Playwright 1.63.0 for tests.\n- **Art direction:** the engine's PS1-style pixel look, card-drawn rigs with accessories, pen-drawn props. No image files.\n- **Animation:** the engine's procedural Humanoid rig, plus game-specific shivers, sinks and braking crouches.\n- **Audio:** the engine's chip synth. Songs are note strings, laughter is an arpeggio, dialogue is Animalese-style blips. No audio files.\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode. The Echo Run reports progress and its time, verified end to end against a mock hub.\n- **Testing:** `node tests/run.mjs`, 156 checks, seeded and repeatable.\n- **Research:** none.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); headless Chromium 1243 via Playwright 1.63.0, WebGL 2 under SwiftShader.\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium.\n- **Usage:** unknown.\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** about 15 in the first build. This round added none that I recorded, but the Comic cel and Pixel filters fail in this renderer.\n- **Critical or game-breaking:** five in the first build: a crash opening Room 7, the black frame from the cel filter, two Rime gates that could lock a run, and a junction that committed or stalled on its own.\n- **Most helpful test:** the Node playthrough of each area. It runs with no page and stops at the first soft-lock, stall or crash.\n- **Least helpful test:** checking single screenshots. The browser flows were flaky with fixed waits until they polled for the expected scene.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the 3D module's fixed cameras and card-drawn rigs, with the pause menu, settings and saves for free.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** yes. I guessed particle argument orders, the pen box centre, and the cel and pixel filters, which go black here. A pause-menu item does not close the menu, so Dev Mode needed `shell.hide()`.\n- **Most important thing I built myself:** the rail walker with junctions and gates, the Whiteout AI and scan, the persona abilities, the NPC and dossier flow, the bot and the test harness.\n- **Hardest part:** working out the 3D API from its header, and the slow shader builds when scenes switch under a software renderer.\n- **Engine changes:** one S7 patch, adding accessories (goggles, scarves, moustaches, beards) to the Humanoid head drawing. Needed because the card rig had no accessory slots.\n- **One change I'd make:** let a pause-menu callback close the menu by default, or document that it must call `shell.hide()`.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** concrete deliverables, file names, the four report sections, and the one-command test rule.\n- **Confusing:** STAGE asks me to follow PLAN.md, which is about 2,100 lines and asks for engine patches and seven full personas. TASK.md sets a feature-complete bar, and it isn't clear which plan details are required.\n- **Hardest:** fitting the plan into one session. It describes a game several times this size.\n- **What I'd change:** give the plan a must, should and cut list, a size budget, and say which engine patches are optional."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1721,"cache_read_input_tokens":490810,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1721},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bb246035-72d8-4ccb-80ef-f75810865350","uuid":"5b8131a1-4428-48d6-92a6-bac1c07aad4a","timestamp":"2026-11-04T11:19:57.217Z","request_id":"req_011CghoDgbBuXqdHdCgPQqbU"}
